; V: TODO: A lot... So much to re-order and cleanup...
; I must recalculate everything, once the full code cleanup and optimization is done.
; Currently, all infos are incorrect due to the massive amount of changes I have done into the code.
; I apologise for the inconvenience, I am doing my best to clean everything to make sense again.
;

; Raster's Warnings:
;
; 1. RMT player routine needs 19 reserved bytes in the zero page that are not accessed
;    from any other routines) as well as cca 1KB of memory before the "PLAYER"
;    address for frequency tables and functionary variables. It's:
;	  a) from PLAYER-$03c0 to PLAYER for stereo RMTplayer
;    b) from PLAYER-$0320 to PLAYER for mono RMTplayer
;
; 2. RMT player routine MUST (!!!) be compiled from the begin of the memory page.
;    i.e. "PLAYER" address can be $..00 only!
;
; 3. Because of RMTplayer provides a lot of effects, it can spend a lot of CPU time.
;

; Raster's change history: carried over from asm/Unpatched/rmt.a65 (plans/51 U3)
; 10.12.2002
; - speed-change fix - A changed speed is written to v_speed only after all 4 (resp. 8)
;   tracks are done. i.e. if the change is in the first row of a track and a goto moves it
;   to the first row, but the second track has an end (=> all actions in this row are
;   invalid and the next song line is taken), then even the speed change from the first row
;   of the first track does not take effect

; 14.12.2002
; - more tracks - Instead of the original tracks 0-$7f extended to 0-$fd ($fe is jump, $ff
;   empty track) the module header gained 2 bytes - it now holds a pointer to the array of
;   low bytes of the track pointers and (in addition) a pointer to the array of high bytes
;   of the track pointers

; 14.12.2002
; - filter and 16-bit bass rework - If a track's resulting volume is 0 (no noise component),
;   neither filtering nor 16-bit bass is applied for that generator => the other generator
;   is not blocked (for the filter or for the low byte of the 16-bit bass) and it can play
;   its own content normally, as its track says (note: this cost 56 bytes of code (stereo
;   56=8x7 bytes, mono 28=4x7 bytes))

; 14.12.2002
; - basstab1 shift - shifted by 8 tones and the lowest 8 filled in with ones an octave
;   higher this tunes bass 1 to everything else (note: bass 2 is correct as it is)

; 21.12.2002
; - command 2 fixed - frequency shift (the bug: it had no effect combined with table shifts)

; 21.12.2002
; - the rmt_set_pokey routine reworked separately for stereo and for mono

; 25.12.2002
; - parameter order in the header changed:
;	p_instrstable		org *+2		;203-4
;	p_trackslbstable	org *+2		;205-6
;	p_trackshbstable	org *+2		;207-8
;	p_song				org *+2		;209-210

; 28.12.2002
; - extended pause specification. If the top two bits are 00 it behaves as before and the
;   pause is given by the next byte; if those two bits are >00 they directly give a pause of
;   1, 2 or 3 rows and the next byte is not used (=> considerable size saving in the
;   resulting RMT files!!!)

; 14.01.2003
; - song line number definition fixed (it multiplied by *4 even for STEREO, now MONO is *4,
;   STEREO *8)

; 18.01.2003
; - envelope command $7 added - BaseNote = $XY

; 03.02.2003
; - formatting of the frq and volume tables reworked

; 08.02.2003
; - PLAYER ROUTINE MODIFICATION - INSTRUMENT VERSION 1 support for longer tables, longer
;   envelopes, full AUDCTL control various optimizations happened along the way => 52 bytes
;   shorter!!!

; 12.02.2003
; - RMT BUG FIX - table speed (the first table element played 1/50 shorter => shifted the
;   rest by 1/50 too) optimized while fixing => 3 bytes shorter!

; 22.02.2003
; - command $7 variation added. If the parameter is $80, the "volume only" mode is used.

; 17.04.2003
; - attempt to fix the bug of one skipped envelope processing at the start (17.04.2003) did
;   not help, so commented out again (jsr rmt_p3)

; 27.04.2003
; - another fix attempt (see 17.04.2003), again by adding that jsr rmt_p3 (uncommenting it).
;   OK! It works, but a related fix had to be made in RMTracker too

; 19.01.2004
; - added the options 4 TRACKS STEREO L1 R2 R3 L4 and 4 TRACKS STEREO L1 L2 R3 R4

; 31.01.2004
; - fixed an addition bug (carry into the high byte) when starting the song from the N-th
;   songline.
; - fixed STEREOMODE 2 and 3 so filters and 16-bit bass work correctly there too

; 11.02.2004
; - added FEAT_VOLUMEMIN and improved FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET (by 2 cycles) on every
;   SetUpInstrumentY2
; - added FEAT_TABLEGO

; 15.02.2004
; - various speed/size optimizations (22 bytes saved)

; 16.02.2004-21.02.2004
; - various speed/size optimizations following Jaskier's advice + some further brutally hard
;   optimizations of my own :-)
; - another 40 (!) bytes saved compared to 15.02.2004

; 13.04.2005
; - reworked the check whether the table is to be used

; 26.12.2005
; - FEAT_INSTRSPEED   (=0 => for modules with varying instr. speed 1 to 4; otherwise
;   hardcoded for one instr. speed only)
; - FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED  (if there is _NO_ speed command at all, it is nonzero and holds the
;   main, constant speed)
; - improvement via self-modifying variables ( v_instrspeed, v_maxtracklen, v_audctl,
;   v_audctl2, v_bspeed )

; 17.02.2006
; - FEAT_SFX

; 02.04.2006
; - FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO and FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT

; 16.04.2006
; - vibrato effect optimization

; 13.09.2007
; - fixed the FEAT optimization for Command5 combined with portamento unused anywhere
; - fixed the FEAT optimization for Command6 combined with the filter unused anywhere
; - ultra-brutal size and speed FEAT optimization of the dispatch by command number
; - improved optimization - sometimes trackn_command is not compiled/initialized at all for
;   every command!

; 30.08.2008
; - support for FEAT_GLOBALVOLUMEFADE for RMTGLOBALVOLUMEFADE

; 08.01.2009
; - label for RMTSFXVOLUME (idea by Tebe)
; - filters take priority over 16-bit bass, or over another track
;    e.g. a) if filtering crossed the lower generator of a pair joined for 16-bit bass,
;             then filtering is used and plain 8-bit bass plays instead of the 16-bit bass
;    e.g. b) if filtering is on in g0, g3 is overwritten with the filtered frequency (and g3's volume is zeroed)
; - 16-bit bass takes priority over another track (except a filtered one, see above)
;   e.g. if g1 uses 16-bit bass, it overwrites g0 with the low byte of the 16-bit frequency (and zeroes g0's volume)
; -  The portamento effect uses a transitional frequency between the source and the target tone + effvibrato/shift
;    (but not the tablenote/shift offsets, except for the setportamento 00 command,
;    where tablenote/shift is added when computing the target portamento frequency)
; - Completed
;   - Define frequencies for note 0 and the top notes 61-63 (60 is the last - for noise =0)
;   - Handle uninitialized instruments at the start of an empty track (instrument hb==0 ? skip the instrument)
;   - Initialization of all track variables to 0
;   - Have initial speed in the module header (instead of the default #8)
;   - Handle bit 7 ($80) and 0 ($01= for AUDCTL

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; The following equates must be defined by the caller:
;
; STEREOMODE	equ 0..4	;0 => 4 tracks mono   with one POKEY chip  (L):   L1 L2 L3 L4 (Default)
;							;1 => 8 tracks stereo with two POKEY chips (L/R): L1 L2 L3 L4 R1 R2 R3 R4
;							;2 => 4 tracks mono   with two POKEY chips (L/R): L1 R2 R3 L4
;							;3 => 4 tracks mono   with two POKEY chips (L/R): L1 L2 R3 R4
;							;4 => 4 tracks mono   with two POKEY chips (L/R): LR1 LR2 LR3 LR4

pokey_left  	equ $d200
pokey_right		equ $d210

; RMT FEATures definitions file
; For optimizations of RMT player routine to concrete RMT module only!
	icl "rmt_feat.a65"

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of RMT definitions.
	IFT STEREOMODE==1
TRACKS			equ 8
	ELS
TRACKS			equ 4
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_IS_SIMPLEP
PLAYER			equ $3100		; VUPlayer export driver
	ELS
PLAYER			equ $3400		; Start of the standard player, also used for "tracker.obx". Beware that the memory before it is used, about $400 (1 KB).
	EIF

INSTRPAR		equ 12			; Number of the instrument's "main" parameters => the table starts at byte 12, the envelope after the table end

; RMT ZeroPage addresses
	org 203

p_tis
p_instrstable		org *+2		; ptr to instrument table ptrs
p_trackslbstable	org *+2		; ptr to low byte of track ptrs
p_trackshbstable	org *+2		; ptr to high byte of track ptrs
p_song				org *+2		; ptr to song data

p_ns				org *+2
p_nr				org *+2
p_nt				org *+2
reg1				org *+1
reg2				org *+1
reg3				org *+1
tmp					org *+1

	IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
frqaddcmd2			org *+1
	EIF

	IFT TRACKS>4
		org PLAYER-$400+$40					; $3040
	ELS
		org PLAYER-$400+$e0					; $30e0
	EIF

track_variables
trackn_lo				org *+TRACKS		; Low byte of address for each track's data
trackn_hi				org *+TRACKS		; High byte of address for each track's data
trackn_idx				org *+TRACKS		; Track index
trackn_pause			org *+TRACKS		; Track pause (in rows). 1 = new note, 0 = nothing new
trackn_note				org *+TRACKS		; 0-59
trackn_volume			org *+TRACKS		; vvvv0000
trackn_volumeenvelope	org *+TRACKS		; Patch16-only
trackn_command			org *+TRACKS		; Patch16-only
trackn_effectparameter	org *+TRACKS		; Patch16-only
trackn_shiftfrq			org *+TRACKS

	IFT FEAT_PORTAMENTO
trackn_portafrqc		org *+TRACKS		; Target portamento frequency
trackn_portafrqa		org *+TRACKS		; Current portamento frequency
trackn_portaspeed 	org *+TRACKS			; Portamento speed
trackn_portaspeeda 	org *+TRACKS			; Current portamento speed
trackn_portadepth 	org *+TRACKS			; Portamento depth
	EIF

trackn_instrx2			org *+TRACKS		; Bit pattern "xiiiiii0" for the instrument. With "x=0", a new instrument is set and initialized. With "x=0", no new instrument is set.
trackn_instrdb			org *+TRACKS
trackn_instrhb			org *+TRACKS
trackn_instridx			org *+TRACKS		; 0,3,6,..,45  (3*16-3)
trackn_instrlen			org *+TRACKS		; Instrument length
trackn_instrlop			org *+TRACKS		; The repeat starts there
trackn_instrreachend	org *+TRACKS		; Set to $80 when the instrument end is first reached (volume decays from then on)
trackn_volumeslidedepth org *+TRACKS		; Volume decay
trackn_volumeslidevalue org *+TRACKS		; Current state of the volume decay

	IFT FEAT_VOLUMEMIN
trackn_volumemin		org *+TRACKS		; Minimum volume value while decaying
	EIF

FEAT_EFFECTS equ FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO||FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT
	IFT FEAT_EFFECTS
trackn_effdelay			org *+TRACKS
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO
trackn_effvibratoa		org *+TRACKS		; Current vibrato index
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT
trackn_effshift			org *+TRACKS
	EIF

trackn_tabletypespeed	org *+TRACKS		; Table type $00=notes,$80=frequencies ; 0-$3f table speed

	IFT FEAT_TABLEMODE
trackn_tablemode		org *+TRACKS		; Table mode $00=set,$40=add
	EIF

trackn_tablenote		org *+TRACKS		; Table note shift
trackn_tablea			org *+TRACKS		; Current index
trackn_tableend			org *+TRACKS		; Table length

	IFT FEAT_TABLEGO
trackn_tablelop			org *+TRACKS		; Table repeat
	EIF

trackn_tablespeeda		org *+TRACKS		; The current table speed

	IFT FEAT_FILTER
trackn_filter			org *+TRACKS		; The frequency shift of the filtering generator. POTENTIAL OPTIMIZATION: it is NOT necessary to use all tracks... only channel 1 and 2 will use it to offset the other...
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16		; EXPERIMENTAL METHOD: full 16-bit values, Sawtooth and Filter may also benefit from this approach...
trackn_bass16			org *+TRACKS
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16||FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH
g_flag			org *+TRACKS
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
trackn_audctl		org *+TRACKS
	EIF

trackn_audf		org *+TRACKS
trackn_audc		org *+TRACKS
; v_audctl		org *+1						; The lda #... parameter is overwritten directly in the code
; v_audctl2		org *+1						; The lda #... parameter is overwritten directly in the code
;
;	IFT FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED==0
; v_speed			org *+1					; The parameter of lda #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
;	EIF
v_aspeed		org *+1
; v_bspeed		org *+1						; The buffer speed (until the changed speed is known to apply)
;											; The parameter of lda #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
;	IFT FEAT_INSTRSPEED==0||FEAT_INSTRSPEED>1
; v_instrspeed	org *+1						; The parameter of lda #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
; v_ainstrspeed	org *+1						; The parameter of lda #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
;	EIF
; v_maxtracklen	org *+1						; The parameter of cmp #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
; v_abeat			org *+1					; The parameter of lda #$ff is overwritten directly in the code
track_endvariables

; End of RMT definitions.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the RMT data
; TODO: Maybe this could be moved elsewhere, much like the tuning tables?

	org PLAYER-$0200					; I need to improve the label organization here as well, also do I really need to org there? my memory is hazy, why did even do this...?

	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
; Bit masks to test for AUDCTL lookup tables using the BIT instruction.
AUDCTL_POLY9	dta $80					; Bit 7
AUDCTL_CH1_179	dta $40					; Bit 6
AUDCTL_CH3_179	dta $20					; Bit 5
AUDCTL_JOIN_12	dta $10					; Bit 4
AUDCTL_JOIN_34	dta $08					; Bit 3
AUDCTL_HPF_CH1	dta $04					; Bit 2
AUDCTL_HPF_CH2	dta $02					; Bit 1
AUDCTL_CLOCK15	dta $01					; Bit 0
	EIF

;tabbeganddistor						; The start offsets into "frqtab" and distortion values for the individual instrument distortions
frqtab_hi_tab							; The high-bytes of the frequency tables.
distortion_tab equ *+1					; The POKEY distortion values for the instrument distortion values.
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_A,$00			; Noise 0
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_2,$20			; Noise 2
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_4,$40			; Noise 4
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_A,$a0			; 16-bit bass (if not g1 or g3, then bass tab 1)
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_A,$80			; Noise 8
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_A,$a0			; Pure tones
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_C,$c0			; Bass tab1
	dta >PAGE_DISTORTION_E,$c0			; Bass tab2

	IFT FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO
vibtabbeg
		dta 0,vib1-vib0,vib2-vib0,vib3-vib0
vib0	dta 0						; No vibrato
vib1	dta 1,-1,-1,1				; Small vibrato
vib2	dta 1,0,-1,-1,0,1			; Middle vibrato
vib3	dta 1,1,0,-1,-1,-1,-1,0,1,1	; Big vibrato
vibtabnext
		dta vib0-vib0+0
		dta vib1-vib0+1,vib1-vib0+2,vib1-vib0+3,vib1-vib0+0
		dta vib2-vib0+1,vib2-vib0+2,vib2-vib0+3,vib2-vib0+4,vib2-vib0+5,vib2-vib0+0
		dta vib3-vib0+1,vib3-vib0+2,vib3-vib0+3,vib3-vib0+4,vib3-vib0+5,vib3-vib0+6,vib3-vib0+7,vib3-vib0+8,vib3-vib0+9,vib3-vib0+0
	EIF

	org PLAYER-$0100			; 256 bytes before the player.

; Volume conversion
volumetab
	dta $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00
	dta $00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$00,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01
	dta $00,$00,$00,$00,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$02,$02,$02,$02
	dta $00,$00,$00,$01,$01,$01,$01,$01,$02,$02,$02,$02,$02,$03,$03,$03
	dta $00,$00,$01,$01,$01,$01,$02,$02,$02,$02,$03,$03,$03,$03,$04,$04
	dta $00,$00,$01,$01,$01,$02,$02,$02,$03,$03,$03,$04,$04,$04,$05,$05
	dta $00,$00,$01,$01,$02,$02,$02,$03,$03,$04,$04,$04,$05,$05,$06,$06
	dta $00,$00,$01,$01,$02,$02,$03,$03,$04,$04,$05,$05,$06,$06,$07,$07
	dta $00,$01,$01,$02,$02,$03,$03,$04,$04,$05,$05,$06,$06,$07,$07,$08
	dta $00,$01,$01,$02,$02,$03,$04,$04,$05,$05,$06,$07,$07,$08,$08,$09
	dta $00,$01,$01,$02,$03,$03,$04,$05,$05,$06,$07,$07,$08,$09,$09,$0A
	dta $00,$01,$01,$02,$03,$04,$04,$05,$06,$07,$07,$08,$09,$0A,$0A,$0B
	dta $00,$01,$02,$02,$03,$04,$05,$06,$06,$07,$08,$09,$0A,$0A,$0B,$0C
	dta $00,$01,$02,$03,$03,$04,$05,$06,$07,$08,$09,$0A,$0A,$0B,$0C,$0D
	dta $00,$01,$02,$03,$04,$05,$06,$07,$07,$08,$09,$0A,$0B,$0C,$0D,$0E
	dta $00,$01,$02,$03,$04,$05,$06,$07,$08,$09,$0A,$0B,$0C,$0D,$0E,$0F

; End of the RMT data.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

	org PLAYER

;
; Start of the RMT jump table with official vectors to call.
; The naming follows the Atari OS naming with "v" suffix, for official vectors, e.g. "ciov".
;
; TODO: Finalize the naming of the labels. Use "rmt_" and lowercase for all?

RASTERMUSICTRACKER

	; Initialize
	;
	; Must be run first, to clear memory and initialize the player.
	; Once this is done, run rmt_play afterwards, or rmt_set_pokey if you want to manually time certain things.
	; IN:  <X>=module address low byte, Y=module address high byte, <A>=starting song line(0-255)
	; OUT: <A>=the instrument speed (1= 1 time per VBI (normal), 2 = 2 times per VBI, 3 = 3 times per VBI, ...
rmt_initv
	jmp rmt_init

	; Play
	;
	; "rmt_set_pokey" is called first, then all the play code is ran once.
	; V: Must be called multiple times per frame if the instrument speed is > 1.
	; R: every 1/50 sec, returns the actual instrument speed
	; IN:  n/a
	; OUT: <A>=the current the instrument speed. TODO: JAC! Really? This was in Raster's comment.
	; TODO: JAC! How does this relate to rmt_p3? Rasters original comment clearly states that "rmt_play" is per frame.
	; So it would make sense that rmt_p3 is to be called within a frame to update only the instruments.
rmt_playv
	jmp rmt_play

	; Instruments Envelope Processing
	; Similar to rmt_play, but will also skip rmt_set_pokey and the songlines/tracklines handling.
rmt_play3v
	jmp rmt_p3

rmt_silencev
	; Set Silence
	;
	; Sets all POKEY registers to their initial values.
	; This is also last part of "rmt_init".
	; IN:  n/a
	; OUT: n/a
	jmp rmt_silence

	; Set POKEY Registers
rmt_set_pokeyv
	;
	; Copies the contents of the shadow POKEY registers (v_audctl, v_skctl, trackn_audf,x etc) into the hardware registers.
	; This is call as the first step in "rmt_play".
	; IN:  n/a
	; OUT: n/a
	jmp rmt_set_pokey

	IFT FEAT_SFX
	; Activate Sound Effect
	;
	; Activates a note with a given instrument on a given channel.
	; This overrides the instrument currently played by the song.
	; IN: <A>=note(0,..,60), <X>=channel(0,..,3 in mono or 0,..,7 in stereo), <Y>=instrument*2 (0,2,4,..,126)
		jmp rmt_sfx
	EIF

; End of the RMT jump table.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of rmt_init code.
; A = Starting song line
; X = low byte of the RMT module
; Y = High byte of the RMT module

rmt_init
	stx p_ns
	sty p_ns+1
	IFT FEAT_NOSTARTINGSONGLINE==0
		pha	; Push the start song line to the stack for now (PHA #1).
			; TODO: V: I wonder if I could just use tmp in zeropage instead...
	EIF

;	Clear the track_variables
	IFT [track_endvariables-track_variables]>255
												; There are more than 255 trackn variables, but less than 513.
												; So clear from the front and 256 bytes from the end |>--->----|
		ldy #0
		tya
ri0		sta track_variables,y
		sta track_endvariables-$100,y
		iny
		bne ri0
	ELS
												; Clear from the back  |----<|
		ldy #track_endvariables-track_variables	; Number of bytes to clear
		lda #0
ri0		sta track_variables-1,y					; Shifted down by 1, so n down to 1 suffices and bne can be used
		dey
		bne ri0
	EIF

						; Parse the RMT module data
						; The track length is at offset +4
	ldy #4
	lda (p_ns),y
	sta v_maxtracklen	; Set the maximum track length.

							; The song speed is at offset +5
	iny
	IFT FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED==0
		lda (p_ns),y
		sta v_speed			; Set the default track speed
	EIF

							; The instrument speed is at offset +6
	IFT FEAT_INSTRSPEED==0
		iny					; #6
		lda (p_ns),y
		sta v_instrspeed	; Set the instrument speed
		sta v_ainstrspeed
	ELI FEAT_INSTRSPEED>1
		lda #FEAT_INSTRSPEED
		sta v_ainstrspeed
	EIF

							; The offset +7 is reserved.

							; Copy 4 pointers starting at offset 8, i.e. offsets 8,9; 10,11; 12,13; 14,15.
							; -> InstrumentPtrs[] 	2 bytes
							; -> TracksPtrsLow[]	2 bytes
							; -> TracksPtrsHi		2 bytes
							; -> SongData			2 bytes

	ldy #8					; Starting from offset 8
ri1	lda (p_ns),y
	sta p_tis-8,y
	iny
	cpy #8+8				; Copy 2*4 = 8 bytes
	bne ri1

	IFT FEAT_NOSTARTINGSONGLINE==0
							; Set the starting song line by moving p_song forward
		pla					; Pull the saved start song line from the stack (PLA #1).
		pha					; Push the start song line on the stack (PHA #2A/B).
		IFT TRACKS>4
							; Stereo
							; p_song += song_line * 8
			asl @			; Stereo 8 tracks => every song line has 8 bytes
			asl @
			asl @			; =*8
			clc
			adc p_song		; p_song += offset * 8 (low) part
			sta p_song
			pla				; Pull the saved start song line from the stack (PLA #2A). This keeps carry flag unchanged.
			php				; Push the flags, we will need the carry flag later (#PHP 3A).
			and #$e0		; Top 3 bits
			asl @			; Into carry
			rol @			; Bit 1
			rol @			; Bit 2
			rol @			; Bit 3
		ELS
							; Mono
							; p_song += song_line * 4
			asl @			; Mono 4 tracks => every song line has 4 bytes
			asl @			; =*4
			clc
			adc p_song
			sta p_song
			pla				; PLA 2B!!!
			php				; PHP 3B!!! (saves the carry)
			and #$c0		; Top 2 bits
			asl @			; Into carry
			rol @			; Bit 1
			rol @			; Bit 2
		EIF
		plp					; Pull the saved flags, we need the carry flag (PLP #3A/B).
		adc p_song+1		; The carry flag was set by the low-byte addition.
		sta p_song+1
	EIF								; FEAT_NOSTARTINGSONGLINE==0

;	jsr GetSongLine
;	jsr GetTrackLine
;	jsr InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly	;first-time instrument setup
;	jsr rmt_p3						;fix 27.04.2003 (first call of the p3 part was skipped => 1/50 shift at the start)

	jsr GetSongLine			; Setup the first song line, track line, init new instruments and call rmt_play3.

;	jsr rmt_silence					; OPTIMIZATION: continues directly into rmt_silence
;	lda v_instrspeed				; OPTIMIZATION: <--this load of the value is at the end of rmt_silence
;	rts								; OPTIMIZATION: before the rts instruction.

; End of the rmt_init code.
; Note: rmt_silence will always be executed next via fall-through.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; RMT_SILENCE
; Reset POKEY causes all sound to be stopped

rmt_silence
									; Reset POKEY
	IFT STEREOMODE>0				; For 1, 2 and 3 alike
		lda #0
		sta pokey_left+$8			; AUDCTL
		sta pokey_right+$8
		ldy #3
		sty pokey_left+$f			; SKCTL
		sty pokey_right+$f

		ldy #8						; Clear AUDFx & AUDCx
si1		sta pokey_left+$0,y
		sta pokey_right+$0,y
		dey
		bpl si1
	ELS
		lda #0
		sta pokey_left+$8
		ldy #3
		sty pokey_left+$f
		ldy #8
si1		sta pokey_left+$0,y
		dey
		bpl si1
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_IS_TRACKER 			; Reset the tables pointers.
		lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch1	; Reset the Sawtooth table inversion.
		sta saw_ch1
		lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch3
		sta saw_ch3
		lda #$0A					; Reset the Distortion 6 16-bit pointer.
		sta bass16_pointer
		lda #3						; Reset the SKCTL state to normal.
		sta v_skctl
		sta v_skctl2
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_INSTRSPEED==0			; Return the instrument speed for the fall-through from "rmt_init". Not relevant/guaranteed for "rmt_silence" itself.
		lda #$ff
v_ainstrspeed equ *-1
	ELS
		lda #FEAT_INSTRSPEED
	EIF
	rts

; End of "rmt_silence" code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

GetSongLine		; Get songline, then get track line, then initialize new instruments
	ldx #0								; Set the current beat in to 0.
	stx v_abeat
nn0										; Before jumping to nn0 from elsewhere, ensure that <X>=0.
;   Next line in the song
;	ldx #0						;must start at column 0 and continue 0->7, because a goto can be there
;   on the first pass (via GetSongLine...) x=0, jumping to nn0 from elsewhere requires ldx #0 before the jump

	IFT FEAT_IS_SIMPLEP
		IFT EXPORTXEX					; Simple RMT Player hack for color cycling, change the rasterbar color every new pattern played
			lda loop+1					; The #RASTERBAR color defined will be loaded there specifically
			add #16						; Offset the value by #$10 for a simple color shuffle
			sta loop+1   				; Store back where it was loaded, overwriting the previous value
			lda p_song					; Calculate the songline position below, this is done once every new songline
			sub MODUL+14 				; TODO: relocate this code elsewhere, so toggling it would be easier
			sta v_ord
			lda p_song+1
			sbc MODUL+15
			lsr @
			ror v_ord
			lsr @
			ror v_ord
			IFT TRACKS>4
				lsr @
				ror v_ord
			EIF
		EIF
	EIF

nn1
	txa									; Y:=A:=X 0,1,2,3
	tay
	lda (p_song),y						; Get track info from the songline[y]
	cmp #$fe							; #$FE = Goto songline, #$FF = Empty track
	bcs nn2								; If A >= $FE, branch to nn2
										; <A> = Real track number $00-$fd.

										; Get the ptr to the track data and store it in p_trackslbstable
	tay
	lda (p_trackslbstable),y			; trackn_lo[x] = p_trackslbstable[y]
	sta trackn_lo,x
	lda (p_trackshbstable),y			; trackn_hi[x] = p_trackshbstable[y]
	sta trackn_hi,x

	lda #0
	sta trackn_idx,x					; Reset the track index to 0.

	lda #1
nn1a2 								; Init track,  #1 is a new track, #0 is no new track
	sta trackn_pause,x					; OPTIMIZATION: So it can jump to nn1a2 for an empty track (i.e. must include the $80 -> instrx2,x below)
	lda #$80							; Initialize as "no new instrument" ($80).
	sta trackn_instrx2,x				; Note values "0-60" do not change it, $80 stays there.
	inx
	cpx #TRACKS
	bne nn1

									; Done with data points of a song line, move to the next line
	lda p_song						; p_song += #TRACKS
	clc
	adc #TRACKS
	sta p_song
	bcc GetTrackLine				; Instead of "bcc nn1b", jump straight to GetTrackLine.
	inc p_song+1
; nn1b
;	rts								; The end of GetSongLine.
	jmp GetTrackLine				; The end of GetSongLine. Continues to GetTrackLine to progress the next notes in the track.

nn2									; Track number >= GOTO ($fe) or EMPTY TRACK ($ff)
;	cmp #$fe						; Was already done before jumping here
	beq nn3							; Yes, it is GOTO (#$fe) => branch

nn2a								; Track number is EMPTY TRACK ($ff).
	lda #0							; 0 is the maximum pause length (256).
	beq nn1a2						; Unconditional jump to nn1a2.

nn3									; Track number is GOTO ($fe).
									; Data format: $fe, unused ($00), low/high byte of pointer to the next song line.
	ldy #2
	lda (p_song),y					; lo = p_song[2]
	tax
	iny
	lda (p_song),y					; hi = ptrSongLinex[3]
	sta p_song+1
	stx p_song						; (p_song) = p_song[2,3]
	ldx #0							; <X> must be 0 before jumping to nn0, to process the new song line from #0 (up to 7)
	beq nn0							; Unconditional jump to the next song line.

; Process the next line of a track for all tracks.
GetTrackLine	; Does get trackline (calling GetSongline back if needed), then instrument init

	IFT FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED==0
		lda #$ff					; The speed as immediate operand is is changed by the code.
v_speed equ *-1
		sta v_bspeed				; Store a copy as the buffer speed.
	EIF

	ldx #-1							; Must run from 0 to TRACKS (not the other way), because speeds on the same trackline overwrite each other.
									; And because ENDofTRACK can stop it in any column, so the opposite side would get executed.
oo1
	inx								; <X>=0 to TRACKS-1
;	lda trackn_pause,x				; OPTIMIZATION: If it was 0, is would be an infinite pause. With these lines commented out it will count down from 255 to 1.
;	beq oo1x						; OPTIMIZATION: This works out the same as an infinite pause, because the longest track can have 256 rows
	dec trackn_pause,x
	bne oo1x						; >0 => pause is 1-255.

									; Setup the pointer to the track data.
oo1b
	lda trackn_lo,x					; (p_ns) = trackn_lo/hi[x]
	sta p_ns
	lda trackn_hi,x
	sta p_ns+1
oo1i
	ldy trackn_idx,x				; <Y> = current index into track data (34 ... 12).
	inc trackn_idx,x				; Increment the track index for next call.

	lda (p_ns),y					; vvnnnnnn iiiiiivv		(v=volume,n=note,i=instrument)
	sta reg1						; A track data point:
									; - 0 - 60 = Note, instr and volume data
									; - 61 - Volume only
									; - 62 = Pause/empty line
									; - 63 - Speed, go loop or end
	and #$3f						; 0-63
	cmp #61							; 61-63 are special notes, i.e. commands.
	beq oo1a						; =61, this is the empty note. It only sets the volumne bit not the note and instrument.
	bcs oo2							; >61

									; Not a command so store the note (0-60).
	sta trackn_note,x				; Set the track note.

									; Get the instrument number, multiplied by 2.
	iny
	lda (p_ns),y					; instrx2 = (data & 0xfc) >> 1
	lsr @							; 0iiiiiiX
	and #$3f*2						; 0iiiiii0
	sta trackn_instrx2,x			; Set the track instrument.

oo1a								; Process volume data
	lda #1							; After a note (or a volume change) there is a pause of 1 row
	sta trackn_pause,x				; Got a note.

									; Get the volume
	ldy trackn_idx,x				; <Y> := track index
	inc trackn_idx,x				; Move to the next data point in the track
	lda (p_ns),y
	lsr @
	ror reg1
	lsr @
	ror reg1
	lda reg1
	IFT FEAT_GLOBALVOLUMEFADE
		sec
		sbc #$00			; Self-modified parameter
RMTGLOBALVOLUMEFADE equ *-1
		bcs voig			; >=0
		lda #0				; <0 => must zero it
voig
	EIF
	and #$f0				; vvvv0000
	sta trackn_volume,x		; Sets the volume.
oo1x
	cpx #TRACKS-1
	bne oo1 				; X stays at #TRACKS-1, which is used below

	IFT FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED==0
		lda #$ff			; Set the song speed from the buffer
v_bspeed equ *-1			; The parameter is self-modified
		sta v_speed			; Only now (after all tracks are processed) is it written to the overall speed.
	ELS
		lda #FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED
	EIF
	sta v_aspeed			; And to the current one too

	; End of GetTrackLine => falls through to the instrument initialization with X = #TRACKS - 1 !
	jmp InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly	; X must be equal to #TRACKS-1

oo2										; Note/command is 62 or 63.
	cmp #63
	beq oo63						; =63 => branch

	lda reg1						; note=62 (00pause, byte ; or 01pause =1 row, 10pause =2 rows, 11pause =3 rows )
	and #$c0						; Top two bits
	beq oo62_b						; Zero => the next byte is the pause size => branch

	asl @							;   xy000000 => C y0000000
	rol @							; C y0000000 => C 0000000x
	rol @							; C 0000000x =>   000000xy
	sta trackn_pause,x
	jmp oo1x

oo62_b
	iny
	lda (p_ns),y
	sta trackn_pause,x
	inc trackn_idx,x		; For the next time
	jmp oo1x
oo63
	lda reg1
	IFT FEAT_CONSTANTSPEED==0
		bmi oo63_1X

		iny					; note=63 (+top bit 0) (speed, byte)
		lda (p_ns),y
		sta v_bspeed		; Set the song speed to the buffered speed.
		inc trackn_idx,x	; For next time
		jmp oo1i			; Immediately continues to the next pair in the track
oo63_1X
	EIF
	cmp #255				; 192+63(go) => 255 (=END, ends all tracks and advances in the song)
	beq oo63_11

; note=63 (top two bits 10)
	iny
	lda (p_ns),y
	sta trackn_idx,x
	jmp oo1i			; Immediately continues to the next pair in the track
oo63_11
; note=63 (top two bits 11) (=>byte1=255)
	jmp GetSongLine

p2xrmtp3			; The bmi p2xrmt_p3 a bit below makes use of this
	jmp rmt_p3

p2x0				; Jumped-to only on the next pass of the <X> loop from 7->0
	dex
	bmi p2xrmtp3	; Loop ended, X=-11

;	End of the InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly part => falls through to rmt_p3

InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly		; CAUTION! Before jumping to InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly, ldx #TRACKS-1 must be loaded
p2x1
	ldy trackn_instrx2,x		; Get the instrument number*2 in the current track.
	bmi p2x0					; If bit 7 is set, there is no new instrument to initialize. Process withthe next track.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the RMT_SFX code.

	IFT FEAT_SFX
		jsr SetUpInstrumentY2
		jmp p2x0

rmt_sfx
		sta trackn_note,x			; Set trackn_note.
		lda #$f0					; sfx note volume*16
RMTSFXVOLUME equ *-1				; label for sfx note volume parameter overwriting
		sta trackn_volume,x			; Sets the volume
	EIF							; Fall-through to SetUpInstrumentY2 with <Y> = instrument number *2, <X> = track number

; End of RMT_SFX code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; It is inlined right here
SetUpInstrumentY2				; IN: <Y> holds the instrument number *2, <X> the track number
	lda (p_instrstable),y
	sta trackn_instrdb,x		; Set the instrument table pointer.
	sta p_nt
	iny
	lda (p_instrstable),y
	sta trackn_instrhb,x
	sta p_nt+1

	IFT FEAT_FILTER
;		lda #1					; This is the RMT 1.28 value.
		lda #0					; V: EXPERIMENTAL approach for more precise manipulation of the PWM
		sta trackn_filter,x		; Set the filtering offset value on new notes.
		ora #1					; The value of 1 is expected here, so just provide it I guess
								; TODO: This does not save anything, see below. Rather have "ldy #1" below.
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_TABLEGO			; TABLEGO
		IFT FEAT_FILTER
			tay					; With FEAT_FILTER, reuses <A>=1 via "tay", so <Y>:=1.
		ELS
			ldy #1				; Without FEAT_FILTER, must do "ldy #1"
		EIF
		lda (p_nt),y
		sta trackn_tablelop,x
		iny	; #2
	ELS
		ldy #2
	EIF
; y=2
	lda (p_nt),y
	sta trackn_instrlen,x
; y=2 still
	iny							; #3
	lda (p_nt),y
	sta trackn_instrlop,x
; y=3
	iny							; #4
	lda (p_nt),y
	sta trackn_tabletypespeed,x	; tmss ssss (type mode speed)
	IFT FEAT_TABLETYPE||FEAT_TABLEMODE
		and #$3f				; 00ss ssss -tablespeed $00-$3f
	EIF
	sta trackn_tablespeeda,x
	IFT FEAT_TABLEMODE
		lda (p_nt),y
		and #$40				; 0m00 0000 (mode only)
		sta trackn_tablemode,x
	EIF
; y=4
	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
		iny						; #5
		lda (p_nt),y
		sta trackn_audctl,x		; audctl
		iny						; #6
	ELS
		ldy #6
	EIF
; y=6
	lda (p_nt),y
	sta trackn_volumeslidedepth,x	; Volume decay on every "goto" in the instrument
; y=6 still
	IFT FEAT_VOLUMEMIN
		iny							; #7
		lda (p_nt),y				; mmmm 0000 volume minimum for the volume decay
;	and #$f0					; Not required bits are already 0.
		sta trackn_volumemin,x
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTS
			iny						; #8
		EIF
	ELS							; FEAT_TABLEGO
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTS
			ldy #8
		EIF	; FEAT_EFFECTS
	EIF
; y=8 (careful, Y=8 only with FEAT_EFFECTS !!! (otherwise not needed)
	IFT FEAT_EFFECTS
		lda (p_nt),y				; effdelay
		sta trackn_effdelay,x
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO
			iny						; #9
			lda (p_nt),y			; effvibrato  0000 00vv  ($0-$3)
;			and #$03			; Not required bits are already 0.
			tay
			lda vibtabbeg,y
			sta trackn_effvibratoa,x
		EIF
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT
			ldy #10					; Byte 10
			lda (p_nt),y			; effshift
			sta trackn_effshift,x
		EIF						; FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT
	EIF							; FEAT_EFFECTS

;	Note: byte 11 is free, reserved for future extensions.
;	By now Y holds who-knows-what ;-)

	lda #128						; The volume decay is "rounded" (i.e. it starts from +128/256)
	sta trackn_volumeslidevalue,x
;	lda #$80						; OPTIMIZATION: moved here from below, because A=128 = $80 right now!
	sta trackn_instrx2,x			; OPTIMIZATION: the instrument was just set up, so $80 is raised again to avoid repeated setup
;	lda #0							; OPTIMIZATION
	asl @							; OPTIMIZATION: <A>=$00 (it was $80 before, asl turns that into $00)
	sta trackn_instrreachend,x		; Then on the first instrument "go" it is set to $80 (volume starts decaying from then on)
	sta trackn_shiftfrq,x
; Carry is now always C=1 (after asl of the value 128)

	tay								; <Y>:=<A>=$00, carry stays C=1.
; y=0
	lda (p_nt),y			    	; Carry stays C=1.
	sta trackn_tableend,x			; Carry stays C=1.
;	clc								; Carry stays C=1. Saves 2 cycles compared to "clc:adc #1"
	adc #0							; <A>:=<A>+1 because C=1.
	sta trackn_instridx,x			; The envelope starts 1 byte after the table
;
; And now the remaining parameters
	lda #INSTRPAR
	sta trackn_tablea,x				; Starts from table entry 0 (=byte 12)
	tay								; ldy #INSTRPAR
	lda (p_nt),y					; Note 0 of the instrument table	(=byte 12)
	sta trackn_tablenote,x			; If tableend=0 => only this ever remains

	IFT FEAT_SFX||FEAT_IS_TRACKER
;	The "rts" is mandatory for the tracker binary, else a lot of things break in RMT!
;	Look inside "rmtextra.a65" for the exclusive tracker.obx code
		rts
	ELS
		jmp p2x0		; Process the next channel's instrument.
	EIF

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;
;
; Start of "RMT_PLAY" code.
;
;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Called every 1/50 sec.
rmt_play

rmt_p0

;	Set the POKEY registers.
	jsr rmt_set_pokey

rmt_p1
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;	Are the instruments running faster than VBI?

	IFT FEAT_INSTRSPEED==0||FEAT_INSTRSPEED>1
		dec v_ainstrspeed
		bne rmt_p3					; Continue to the instrument envelope processing
									; (skipping the classic track processing)
	EIF
	IFT FEAT_INSTRSPEED==0
		lda #$ff					; The parameter is self-modified
v_instrspeed	equ *-1
		sta v_ainstrspeed
	ELI FEAT_INSTRSPEED>1
		lda #FEAT_INSTRSPEED
		sta v_ainstrspeed
	EIF


;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rmt_p2								; Track processing
	dec v_aspeed
	bne rmt_p3			; Jump (past the initialization of newly set instruments)
;
	inc v_abeat			; Next beat in the track.

	lda #$ff			; The copy of v_abeat as immediate operand is is changed by the code.
v_abeat equ *-1
	cmp #$ff			; Is it the maximum track length?
v_maxtracklen equ *-1	; Parameter self-modification
	beq p2o3			; Yes => branch
	jmp GetTrackLine	; No, so continue to the next track line. Itself calls GetSongLine when needed
						; and then also calls InitOfNewSetInstrumentsOnly and continues to rmt_p3

p2o3
	jmp GetSongLine		; Get song line, track line, init new instruments and continue to rmt_p3.

;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

rmt_p3							; Envelope processing
	ldx #TRACKS-1				; OPTIMIZATION to 7->0 (x--)  ...for the envelope processing the order may be swapped


;
; V: Aggressive initialization every new player call here, the method was originally done to get the AUDCTL early, but many things can be exploited here the same way.
; Combining the aggressive init and rmt_p3 in 1 thing, this is now an even more aggressive approach!
;
; POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENT: process ALL effect commands here instead... Meaning there won't be workarounds necessary later, for several commands.
; Example: Get AUDCTL early, get effect values early, process instrument accordingly afterwards.
; Doing certain things in a different order might drastically speed up several parts that end up being redundant or even overwritten later during certain effects like AUTOFILTER or BASS16.
; Let's say, process 16-bit here... in such case, there won't be anything stopping the player to know it can safely skip a channel's instrument if it was going to be overwritten anyway...
; This is purely speculation, however, so what is done here currently does the job, at least. This is still very different from the original RMT driver code as it is.
;

dodex
	lda trackn_instrhb,x
	beq dexnext					; An empty instrument has high byte $00. Process the next channel's bytes immediately.
	sta p_ns+1
	lda trackn_instrdb,x
	sta p_ns
	ldy trackn_instridx,x
	lda (p_ns),y					; Get volume byte
	sta trackn_volumeenvelope,x		; Was "sta reg1"
	iny
	lda (p_ns),y					; Get command and distortion byte
	sta trackn_command,x			; Was "sta reg2"
	iny
	lda (p_ns),y					; Get $XY parameter byte
	sta trackn_effectparameter,x	; Was "sta reg3"
	iny
	tya
	cmp trackn_instrlen,x
	bcc pp2
	beq pp2
	lda #$80					; An instrument goto is executed => sets trackn_instrreachend
	sta trackn_instrreachend,x

	lda trackn_instrlop,x
pp2
	sta trackn_instridx,x

	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET&&FEAT_COMMAND7	; POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENT: process the Two-Tone Filter commands here instead, leaving CMD7 only useful for Volume Only checks later
dex_cmd7
		lda trackn_command,x
		and #$70							; Clear distortion and other bits
		cmp #$70							; Command 7?
		bne dexnext							; Skip if not equal
		lda trackn_effectparameter,x
dex_xy
		cmp #$FD							; Failsafe -> Volume Only Mode or SKCTL toggle
		bcs dexnext							; Skip if above or equal #$FD
		sta trackn_audctl,x					; Overwrite the previous value
	EIF

dexnext
	dex
	bpl dodex						; Continue until <X> is negative

; FORCE ALL INSTRUMENTS TO USE THE SAME AUDCTL TO NOT OVERLAP IN PRIORITY
; DOESNT WORK LIKE THAT FUCK, HOW COULD I FORCE A AUDCTL CLEAR ON A CHANNEL ABOVE ONE I AM USING?
; Ideally... what would be even better is to have a global effect channel...
; y'know, like a music tracker? That could also be useful for setting certain
; global values like tempo, note offset, etc.

pp0

; Get AUDCTL as early as possible, properly this time!

	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
		lda trackn_audctl+0
		ora trackn_audctl+1
		ora trackn_audctl+2
		ora trackn_audctl+3
		sta v_audctl

								; Assign flags early here as soon as possible

		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16||FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH
			tay					; Backup the now combined audctl for the flags attribution
			and #1				; 64khz == 0, 15khz == 1 always, the other flags will then take priority over this
			sta g_flag+0		; ch1
			sta g_flag+1		; ch2
			sta g_flag+2		; ch3
			sta g_flag+3		; ch4
			tya					; Get the AUDCTL back for the BIT tests below
pp0_a
			bit AUDCTL_CH1_179
			beq pp0_d			; BNE => 1.79mhz, BEQ => Nothing, skip the next BIT test
			bit AUDCTL_JOIN_12
			bne pp0_b			; BNE => 16-bit, BEQ => 1.79mhz
			ldx #$40			; 1.79mhz pointer
			bne pp0_c			; Unconditional branch
pp0_b
			ldx #$80			; 16-bit pointer
			stx g_flag+1		; Flag set in ch2
			dex					; #$80 becomes #$7F
pp0_c
			stx g_flag+0		; Flag set in ch1
pp0_d
			bit AUDCTL_CH3_179
			beq pp0_g			; BNE => 1.79mhz, BEQ => Nothing, skip the next BIT test
			bit AUDCTL_JOIN_34
			bne pp0_e			; BNE => 16-bit, BEQ => 1.79mhz
			ldx #$40			; 1.79mhz pointer
			bne pp0_f			; Unconditional branch
pp0_e
			ldx #$80			; 16-bit pointer
			stx g_flag+3		; Flag set in ch4
			dex					; #$80 becomes #$7F
pp0_f
			stx g_flag+2		; Flag set in ch3
pp0_g
		EIF

		IFT TRACKS>4			; Stereo, same code again for offset +4
			lda trackn_audctl+4
			ora trackn_audctl+5
			ora trackn_audctl+6
			ora trackn_audctl+7
			sta v_audctl2

			IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16||FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH
				tay				; Backup the now combined audctl for the flags attribution
				and #1			; 64khz == 0, 15khz == 1 always, the other flags will then take priority over this
				sta g_flag+0+4	; ch1
				sta g_flag+1+4	; ch2
				sta g_flag+2+4	; ch3
				sta g_flag+3+4	; ch4
				tya				; Get the AUDCTL back for the BIT tests below
pp0_h
				bit AUDCTL_CH1_179
				beq pp0_k		; BNE => 1.79mhz, BEQ => Nothing, skip the next BIT test
				bit AUDCTL_JOIN_12
				bne pp0_i		; BNE => 16-bit, BEQ => 1.79mhz
				ldx #$40		; 1.79mhz pointer
				bne pp0_j		; Unconditional branch
pp0_i
				ldx #$80		; 16-bit pointer
				stx g_flag+1+4	; Flag set in ch2
				dex				; #$80 becomes #$7F
pp0_j
				stx g_flag+0+4	; Flag set in ch1
pp0_k
				bit AUDCTL_CH3_179
				beq pp0_n		; BNE => 1.79mhz, BEQ => Nothing, skip the next BIT test
				bit AUDCTL_JOIN_34
				bne pp0_l		; BNE => 16-bit, BEQ => 1.79mhz
				ldx #$40		; 1.79mhz pointer
				bne pp0_m		; Unconditional branch
pp0_l
				ldx #$80		; 16-bit pointer
				stx g_flag+3+4	; Flag set in ch4
				dex				; #$80 becomes #$7F
pp0_m
				stx g_flag+2+4	; Flag set in ch3
pp0_n
			EIF
		EIF
	ELS
		lda #0
		sta v_audctl
		IFT TRACKS>4
			sta v_audctl2
		EIF
	EIF

pp0_o
	ldx #TRACKS-1					; Must get the tracks value again before the next part

pp1							; Copying the values to the zeropage to make things faster... but not all bytes need this...

; OPTIMIZATION: reg1 is now free to be used for a different purpose!

	lda trackn_instrhb,x
	bne pp1b						; Continue if not equal
	jmp ppnext						; Skip this channel and process the next one
pp1b
	lda g_flag,x					; AUDCTL flags
	sta reg1						; Backup to the zeropage for quicker accesses
	lda trackn_command,x			; Command and distortion byte
	sta reg2						; Backup to the zeropage for quicker accesses
	lda trackn_effectparameter,x	; $XY parameter byte
	sta reg3						; Backup to the zeropage for quicker accesses

	lda trackn_volumeenvelope,x		; Volume envelope byte

	IFT TRACKS>4
		cpx #4						; Is it channel 4-7?
		bcc pp2s					; No, it is 0-3 => branch and use 0000 llll directly
		lsr @						; Yes => shift rrrrllll
		lsr @
		lsr @
		lsr @						; =>0000rrrr
pp2s
	EIF

	and #$0f						; 0000llll (low 4 bits)
	ora trackn_volume,x				; vvvv0000
	tay
	lda volumetab,y
	sta tmp							; Backup the final volume (0-15) in "tmp". This is faster than PHA/PLA.
									; It will be used to compute the AUDC value a bit later.
									
;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the tuning tables code.

;
; POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENT: make a JMP table indexed by X, instead of these dumb 1 by 1 checks... now done?
; ANOTEHR POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENT: get the combined Distortion and Volume value as soon as possible, then get the tables pointer loaded...
;
; This may potentially debloat a lot of this part, and make things much faster as well
; AUDCTL BIT bytes could also be snuck in between the JMPs, replacing the NOPs, saving some space too!
; In fact, a lot of the things here need to get improved a lot more... 6502 ASM is hard!!!
;

do_tuning_tables
	lda reg2					; Get dstortion and command.
	and #$0e					; Only keep the distortion bits.
	tay							; Will be used for the tables MSB pointer, and the Distortion itself

	IFT FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET	; !!!! big block begins here

		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16
			lda reg1			; Load the channel flag for the initial 16-bit checks
			bmi get_16bit_flag	; 16-bit MSB flag detected, jump and finish there immediately
			cmp #$7F			; 16-bit LSB flag
			bcc check_index		; If not #$7F, the index checks will take care of everything else

								; lda trackn_bass16,x	; get the LSB pitch value
								; sta trackn_audf,x	; and write into the appropriate channel! -- BUG! This may be skipped entirely, unfortunately

			lda #0				; The 16-bit LSB flag was set, so first load 0
			sta trackn_audc,x	; Then mute the channel
								; sta trackn_bass16,x	; and reset the LSB value before the next call-- BUG? if this is not done, the channel seems to outputs garbage on certain commands, why does this happen?
			jmp ppnext			; And finish this one early, there is nothing else to do here!
		EIF

check_index						; IMPROVEMENT: the flags system should work much better this time!
		txa
		IFT TRACKS>4			; Stereo mode
			cpx #4				; Are we in the right POKEY channels?
			bcc check_index_a	; If x is below 4, we are not
			sbc #4				; Carry is set, 4 will be subtracted
		EIF
check_index_a
		asl @
		asl @
		sta c_index+1
		lda reg1				; Load the channel flag back in memory for the upcoming checks
c_index	bcc *
		jmp check_ch1
		nop
		jmp check_ch2
		nop
		jmp check_ch3
		nop
		jmp check_ch4

check_ch1
		IFT FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH
			cmp #$40				; 1.79mhz flag
			bne get_15khz_flag		; No Sawtooth and no 1.79mhz if not equal
			cpy #$0A				; Distortion A?
			bne store_tables_lsb	; No Sawtooth if not equal, but the 1.79mhz flag is set!
			lda tmp					; Volume value backup
			beq check_ch1_a			; No Sawtooth if the volume is 0
			lda reg2				; Commands backup
			bpl check_ch1_a			; No Sawtooth if the AUTOFILTER command is off
			jmp do_sawtooth			; If all checks passed, process the Sawtooth code from here
check_ch1_a
			lda reg1
			bpl store_tables_lsb	; 1.79mhz flag is still set, finish like normal
		ELS							; No Sawtooth code
			bpl check_ch3			; The 1.79mhz flag is the same regardless of the channel used, saves some bytes
		EIF

check_ch2
		IFT FEAT_BASS16
			cpy #$06			; Distortion 6?
			bne get_15khz_flag	; If not equal, no BASS16
			lda tmp				; Volume value backup
			beq reload_flag		; If the volume is 0, no BASS16
			lda #$50			; JOIN_12 + CH1_179 bits
			jmp do_bass16		; If all checks passed, process the BASS16 code from here
		ELS
			bpl get_15khz_flag	; There is nothing else to check, unconditional
		EIF

check_ch3
		cmp #$40				; 1.79mhz flag
		beq store_tables_lsb	; Yes! finish from there
		bne get_15khz_flag		; There is nothing else to check, unconditional

check_ch4
		IFT FEAT_BASS16
			cpy #$06			; Distortion 6?
			bne get_15khz_flag	; If not equal, no BASS16
			lda tmp				; Volume value backup
			beq reload_flag		; If the volume is 0, no BASS16
			lda #$28			; JOIN_34 + CH3_179 bits
			jmp do_bass16		; If all checks passed, process the BASS16 code from here
reload_flag
			lda reg1			; Reload the channel flag if no longer in memory before the 15khz checks!
		EIF

; from here, the flag MUST be in memory, so reload it unless it is 100% certain it is ready to use!

get_15khz_flag
		and #1					; #$01 == 15khz flag, unconditional
		beq store_tables_lsb	; #$00 == 64khz flag, unconditional

check_15khz
		cpy #$0C				; Are we in Distortion C/E?
		bcs check_15khz_b		; If equal or above, use the Distortion C 15khz table, else, use the Distortion A 15khz table
		lda #<frqtabpure_15khz	; Distortion A 15khz table LSB
		bcc check_15khz_c		; Carry flag still set
check_15khz_b
		lda #<frqtabbuzzy_15khz	; Distortion C 15khz table LSB
check_15khz_c
		sta p_nr				; Low byte for setting the frequency from the table
		lda #>PAGE_EXTRA_0		; Tables MSB pointer, it's the same one regardless of the table used
		bne store_tables_lsb_a	; Unconditional

		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT
goto_bass16
			jmp do_bass16_c		; Go directly in the BASS16 code handling the CMD6 hijack, skipping the AUDCTL update
get_16bit_flag
			cpy #$06			; Distortion 6?
			beq goto_bass16		; Yes! finish from there
		EIF

	EIF			; FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET

store_tables_lsb
	sta p_nr					; Tables LSB pointer, divided in slices of 64 bytes each
	lda frqtab_hi_tab,y			; 64khz, 1.79mhz and 16-bit all use their flag directly, #$00, #$40 and #$80 are valid pointers!

store_tables_lsb_a
	sta p_nr+1					; Tables MSB pointer, which is the memory page used for tables divided based on their Distortion

store_tables_lsb_b
	lda tmp						; Get volume value backup.
	ora distortion_tab,y		; Merge the Distortion and Volume values
store_tables_lsb_c
	sta trackn_audc,x			; Update the channel's AUDC for the next rmt_set_pokey subroutine call

; End of tuning tables code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the instruments effect code.

InstrumentsEffects				; X holds the track number 7-0
	IFT FEAT_EFFECTS
		lda trackn_effdelay,x
		beq ei2					; =0 => no effects
		cmp #1					; The delay decreases down to one at most
		bne ei1					; The delay decreases down to one at most
		lda trackn_shiftfrq,x
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTFSHIFT
			clc
			adc trackn_effshift,x
		EIF
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO
			clc
			ldy trackn_effvibratoa,x	; Active vibrato index
			adc vib0,y
		EIF
		sta trackn_shiftfrq,x
		IFT FEAT_EFFECTVIBRATO
			lda vibtabnext,y	; Vibrato step
			sta trackn_effvibratoa,x
		EIF
		jmp ei2
ei1
		dec trackn_effdelay,x	; The delay is greater than 1, so decrease it
ei2
	EIF							; FEAT_EFFECTS
; Table
	ldy trackn_tableend,x
	cpy #INSTRPAR+1				; <13?
	bcc ei3						; Yes => the table length is <= 0 => skip it all

	lda trackn_tablespeeda,x	; Speed
	bpl ei2f					; >=0  => no movement in the table
ei2c
	tya							; Advance the table's current index
	cmp trackn_tablea,x
	bne ei2c2					; Not at the end yet
	IFT FEAT_TABLEGO
		lda trackn_tablelop,x	; Table lop
	ELS
		lda #INSTRPAR			; All loops always jump to 0 => fixed start of all loops (byte 12)
	EIF
	sta trackn_tablea,x
	bne ei2a					; ! always branches
ei2c2
	inc trackn_tablea,x			; Advance to the next
ei2a

	lda trackn_instrdb,x
	sta p_nt
	lda trackn_instrhb,x
	sta p_nt+1
	ldy trackn_tablea,x			; 0-7
	lda (p_nt),y
	IFT FEAT_TABLEMODE
		ldy trackn_tablemode,x	; Table mode? ($00/$40)
		beq ei2e				; ==$00 => sets tablenote/tableshift
		clc						; ==$40 => adds to tablenote/tableshift
		adc trackn_tablenote,x
ei2e
	EIF
	sta trackn_tablenote,x
	lda trackn_tabletypespeed,x	; tmss ssss
	IFT FEAT_TABLETYPE||FEAT_TABLEMODE
		and #$3f				; 00ss ssss - speed only
	EIF
ei2f
	sec
	sbc #1
	sta trackn_tablespeeda,x

ei3
	lda trackn_instrreachend,x	; Has the instrument end ever been reached?
	bpl ei4						; Bit $80 == 0 => not yet => branch
								; Bit $80 == 1  => yes => volumeslide is subtracted
	lda trackn_volume,x			; Top 4 bits
	beq ei4						; Volume already zero => branch
	IFT FEAT_VOLUMEMIN
		cmp trackn_volumemin,x	; At the minimum?
		beq ei4					; Yes => branch (no more decay)
		bcc ei4					; Even smaller => branch (no more decay)
	EIF
	tay							; Stashes the volume into Y
	lda trackn_volumeslidevalue,x
	clc
	adc trackn_volumeslidedepth,x
	sta trackn_volumeslidevalue,x
	bcc ei4						; carry==0 => branch
	tya							; (carry=1)
	sbc #16						; trackn_volume uses the top 4 bits (multiples of 16)
	sta trackn_volume,x

ei4
; </InstrumentsEffects>
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
		lda #0
		sta frqaddcmd2			; Initialization of the frequency shift by command 2
	EIF
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND1||FEAT_COMMAND2||FEAT_COMMAND3||FEAT_COMMAND4||FEAT_COMMAND5||FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
; Are there any commands other than COMMAND 0 at all?
; Yes, there are!
		lda reg2
		and #$70					; Mask out non-relevent bits for command "0ccc 0000".
		IFT 1==[FEAT_COMMAND1+FEAT_COMMAND2+FEAT_COMMAND3+FEAT_COMMAND4+FEAT_COMMAND5+FEAT_COMMAND6+FEAT_COMMAND7]
									; There is exactly one command other than command 0
			beq cmd0				; If it is zero after and #$70, cmd0 is handled (which sits after all the commands)
									; and after this, only that single command present gets compiled (the only one other than command 0)
		ELS	; There are two or more commands besides command 0 (i.e. 3 or more in total)
			lsr @
			lsr @					; /4 (=>0,4,8,...)
			sta jmx+1
jmx			bcc *
			jmp cmd0
			nop
			jmp cmd1
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND2||FEAT_COMMAND3||FEAT_COMMAND4||FEAT_COMMAND5||FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd2
			EIF
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND3||FEAT_COMMAND4||FEAT_COMMAND5||FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd3
			EIF
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND4||FEAT_COMMAND5||FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd4
			EIF
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND5||FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd5
			EIF
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND6||FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd6
			EIF
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND7
				nop
				jmp cmd7
			EIF
		EIF
	EIF						; Any commands other than COMMAND 0

; End of instruments effects code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the instruments commands code.
; Note: The instrument effects code falls through to this.

; cmd0 comes last of the commands as an optimization, so it can continue straight to pp9

cmd1							; Play FRQ n
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND1
		lda reg3
		IFT FEAT_PORTAMENTO
			jmp pp10d			; Fixes Portamento overwriting the CMD1 command (absolute pitch)
		ELS
			jmp cmd0c			; OPTIMIZATION: after cmd0c it does sta trackn_audf,x and continues straight on without the jump to pp9
		EIF
	EIF

cmd2							; Play NOTE + FRQ_n		[+shiftfrq]
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
		lda reg3
		sta frqaddcmd2			; Frequency shift by command 2
		lda trackn_note,x
		jmp cmd0a
	EIF

cmd3							; NOTE = NOTE + NOTE_n	;play CMD 0 00
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND3
		lda trackn_note,x
		clc
		adc reg3
		sta trackn_note,x
		jmp cmd0a
	EIF

cmd4							; shiftfrq = shiftfrq + FRQ_n	;play CMD 0 00
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND4
		lda trackn_shiftfrq,x
		clc
		adc reg3
		sta trackn_shiftfrq,x
		lda trackn_note,x
		jmp cmd0a
	EIF

cmd5							; Set destination portamento XY (X-speed, Y-depth), XY==00 =>set actual_portamento_frq=destination_portamento_frq
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND5&&FEAT_PORTAMENTO
		IFT FEAT_TABLETYPE
			lda trackn_tabletypespeed,x		; What table type is it?
			bpl cmd5a1						; Bit 7 is 0: note shift mode (notes table mode)
			ldy trackn_note,x				; Bit 8 is 1: frequency shift mode.

			IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16
				lda reg1					; Flag in memory
				bpl cmd5a0					; Positive means no 16-bit mode active
				tya
				asl @						; Offset for the 16-bit addressing
				tay
				iny							; 16-bit MSB offset
			EIF

cmd5a0
			lda (p_nr),y					; This is the actual note base frequency, or AUDF.
			clc								; Clear carry flag.
			bpl cmd5a0b						; If the value is positive, branch and finish there
cmd5a0a
			adc trackn_tablenote,x			; Here as a frequency
			bvs cmd5ax
			bmi cmd5ax
			lda #$FF						; If overflow, force #$FF!
			bne cmd5ax
cmd5a0b
			adc trackn_tablenote,x
			bvs cmd5ax
			bpl cmd5ax
			lda #0							; If overflow, force #$00!
			beq cmd5ax						; Unconditional branch.
;			jmp cmd5ax						; Process the remaining the code there
		EIF									; FEAT_TABLETYPE

cmd5a1
		lda trackn_note,x					; Current note
		clc									; Clear carry
		adc trackn_tablenote,x				; Add the note from table
		cmp #61								; Max possible note
		bcc cmd5a2							; Branch if lower than 61, finish with it
		lda #63								; else, max possible note value
cmd5a2
		tay

		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16	; TODO: fix the proper 16-bit mode, as well as the Sawtooth and/or AUTOFILTER when combined as well
			lda reg1						; Flag in memory
			bpl cmd5a3						; Positive means no 16-bit mode active
			tya
			asl @							; Offset for the 16-bit addressing
			tay
			iny								; 16-bit MSB offset
		EIF

cmd5a3
		lda (p_nr),y						; Actual note from the frequency table.
cmd5ax
		sta trackn_portafrqc,x				; Set the target portamento frequency
		ldy reg3							; Get the #$XY instrument parameter.
		bne cmd5a							; Jump aheead if not zero.
		sta trackn_portafrqa,x				; Else, set the current portamento frequency.
											; BUG: Portamento is never initialized if the #$XY parameter is not on the very first player call!
cmd5a
		lda trackn_portafrqa,x				; Is the current frequency set to 0?
		bne cmd5b							; If not, it's most likely correctly set
		tay									; Force the #$XY parameter to 0 to force Portamento to not run
		sta reg3							; It will be called again further below
		lda trackn_portafrqc,x				; Target frequency previously set
		sta trackn_portafrqa,x				; Overwrite forced on the current frequency, to avoid the "pitch from 0" bug
cmd5b
		tya									; Transfer the #$XY parameter to the accumulator
		lsr @								; Divide by 16
		lsr @
		lsr @
		lsr @
		sta trackn_portaspeed,x		; Set the portamento speed with the new value
		sta trackn_portaspeeda,x
		lda reg3					; #$XY parameter again
		and #$0f					; Only keep the Y values
		sta trackn_portadepth,x		; Set the portamento pitch offset to process each step
		lda trackn_note,x			; Current note
		jmp cmd0a					; Finish everything else like normal from there
	ELI FEAT_COMMAND5
; Command 5 is present, but portamento is never used
		lda trackn_note,x			; Behaves like a standard command 0
		jmp cmd0a					; Without shifting the note by the parameter
	EIF

cmd6	; filtershiftfrq = filtershiftfrq + FRQ_n
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND6&&FEAT_FILTER	; EXPERIMENTAL: do NOT stack the effects together, and start the offset at 0!
		lda reg3					; Get the $XY parameter for the effect command.
;		clc							; Clear the carry flag.
;		adc trackn_filter,x			; Add it to the frequency offset currently in memory.
		sta trackn_filter,x			; Overwrite the frequency offset with the new value.
		lda trackn_note,x			; Get the current note for this instrument.
		jmp cmd0a					; Process the remaining of CMD0 without adding the $XY value to it.
	ELI FEAT_COMMAND6				; CMD6 alone is essentially no command at all, regardless of the $XY value.
; Command 6 is present, but the filter is never used
		lda trackn_note,x			; Behaves like a standard command 0
		jmp cmd0a					; Without shifting the note by the parameter
	EIF

cmd7	; NOTE = NOTE_n				;play CMD 0 00
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND7
		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE||FEAT_COMMAND7VOLUMEONLY
			IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
				lda reg3
				cmp #$fd			; #$fd toggles Two-Tone off
				bcc cmd7f			; No values will match if less than this, failsafe in case the BPL above didn't catch it
				beq cmd7b			; Turn off the Two-Tone Filter if equal
				cmp #$fe			; #$fe toggles Two-Tone on
				beq cmd7c			; Turn on the Two-Tone Filter if equal
				IFT FEAT_COMMAND7VOLUMEONLY
					bne cmd7a		; #$FF sets volume only mode, and will always be that value here, unconditional branching
				ELS
					bne cmd7f		; Skip ahead, and don't set volume only mode either
				EIF
cmd7b
				lda #3				; Disable the Two-Tone Filter with this value
				bne cmd7d			; Unconditional
cmd7c
				lda #$8B			; Enable the Two-Tone Filter with this value
cmd7d
				IFT TRACKS>4
					cpx #4
					bcc cmd7e		; Less than 4
					sta v_skctl2	; SKCTL, Right POKEY
					bcs cmd7f		; Carry flag still set, unconditional
				EIF
cmd7e
				sta v_skctl			; SKCTL, Left POKEY
			ELS
				IFT FEAT_COMMAND7VOLUMEONLY
					lda reg3
					cmp #$FF
					beq cmd7a		; Set volume only mode if equal
				EIF
			EIF
cmd7f
			lda trackn_note,x
			jmp cmd0a
cmd7a
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND7VOLUMEONLY
				lda trackn_audc,x
				ora #$f0			; 111 1 vvvv
				sta trackn_audc,x
				bne cmd7f			; Unconditional branch.
			EIF
		ELS
			lda trackn_note,x
			jmp cmd0a
		EIF
	EIF

; cmd0 comes last of the commands as an optimization, so it can continue straight to pp9
cmd0							; Play NOTE + NOTE_n		[+shiftfrq]
	lda trackn_note,x
	clc
	adc reg3
cmd0a
	IFT FEAT_TABLETYPE			; Type? (the top bit decides)
		ldy trackn_tabletypespeed,x	
		bmi cmd0b				; >=$80 => frequency => branch
	EIF
	clc
	adc trackn_tablenote,x		; Table note shift
	cmp #61						; Note range 0-60 (60 included)
	bcc cmd0a1					; OK (0-60) => branch
	lda #0
	sta trackn_audc,x			; Silence
	lda #63						; More than 60 => note 63
cmd0a1
	tay

cmd0a1_a
	IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16
		lda reg1
		beq cmd0a3			; No 16-bit flag set
		bpl cmd0a2			; Sawtooth flag set (maybe)
		tya
		asl @				; Offset for the 16-bit addressing!!!
		tay
		iny					; Offset to load the MSB value first
		lda (p_nr),y
		dey					; Offset to load the LSB value later
		sta trackn_audf,x	; Get and store the MSB channel early
		lda trackn_shiftfrq,x
		IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
			clc
			adc frqaddcmd2
		EIF
		sta tmp			; Get and store the frequency shift early, combined if CMD2 is also enabled
		bmi cmd0a1sub	; Will subtract 1 from the MSB if negative on overflow
cmd0a1add
		lda (p_nr),y
		clc
		adc tmp
		sta trackn_bass16-1,x	; LSB channel
		bcc cmd0a1adddone		; No overflow, done
		inc trackn_audf,x		; Increment the MSB if the value went past #$FF
cmd0a1adddone
		jmp pp9					; Done

cmd0a1sub
		lda (p_nr),y
		clc
		adc tmp
		sta trackn_bass16-1,x	; LSB channel
		bcs cmd0a1adddone		; No overflow, done
		dec trackn_audf,x		; Decrement the MSB if the value went past #$00

cmd0a1subdone
		jmp pp9					; Done
	EIF

cmd0a2	; Sawtooth is so unlikely to even range the low #$FF frequencies that applying the vibrato fixes is pointless!
	IFT FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH&&FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
		cmp #$41				; 1.79mhz => Sawtooth?
		bne cmd0a3				; No Sawtooth for sure

		lda (p_nr),y			; Note frequency table
		clc
		adc trackn_shiftfrq,x
		IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
			clc
			adc frqaddcmd2	; Possible shift by command 2
		EIF
		sta trackn_audf+2,x	; Since we're in channel 1 of either POKEY, offset +2 will always be the 3rd channel
		pla					; Get the second sawtooth pointer back from stack
		sta p_nr			; Update the tables pointer to the other sawtooth table
	EIF

cmd0a3
;	lda (p_nr),y
;	clc
;	adc trackn_shiftfrq,x
;	IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
;	clc
;	adc frqaddcmd2
;	EIF

	lda trackn_shiftfrq,x	; Vibrato, and some other shifts use this value
	IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
		clc					; Clear carry
		adc frqaddcmd2		; If the CMD2 feature is also enabled, add that value as well
	EIF
	sta tmp					; Temporary, for faster operation below
cmd0a3a
	lda (p_nr),y			; This is the actual note base frequency, or AUDF
	clc						; Clear carry
	bpl cmd0a3c				; If the value is positive, branch and finish there
cmd0a3b
	adc tmp
	bvs cmd0a4
	bmi cmd0a4
	lda #$FF				; If overflow, force #$FF!
	bne cmd0a4
cmd0a3c
	adc tmp
	bvs cmd0a4
	bpl cmd0a4
	lda #0					; If overflow, force #$00!
cmd0a4

	IFT FEAT_TABLETYPE
		jmp cmd0c			; OPTIMIZATION: after cmd0c it does sta trackn_audf,x and continues straight on without the jump to pp9
cmd0b
		cmp #61				; Note range 0-60
		bcc cmd0b1			; OK (0-60) => branch
		lda #0
		sta trackn_audc,x	; Silence
		lda #63				; More than 60 => note 63
cmd0b1
		tay

cmd0b1_a
		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16
			lda reg1
			beq cmd0b3			; No 16-bit flag set
			bpl cmd0b2			; Sawtooth flag set (maybe)
			tya
			asl @				; Offset for the 16-bit addressing!!!
			tay
			iny					; Offset to load the MSB value first
			lda (p_nr),y
			dey					; Offset to load the LSB value later
			sta trackn_audf,x	; Get and store the MSB channel early
			lda trackn_shiftfrq,x
			clc
			adc trackn_tablenote,x
			clc
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
				clc
				adc frqaddcmd2
			EIF
			sta tmp				; Get and store the frequency shift early, combined if CMD2 is also enabled
			bmi cmd0b1sub		; Will subtract 1 from the MSB if negative on overflow
cmd0b1add
			lda (p_nr),y
			clc
			adc tmp
			sta trackn_bass16-1,x	; LSB 16-bit channel, update early here
			bcc cmd0b1adddone		; No overflow, done
			inc trackn_audf,x		; Increment the MSB if the value went past #$FF
cmd0b1adddone
			jmp pp9					; Done
cmd0b1sub
			lda (p_nr),y
			clc
			adc tmp
			sta trackn_bass16-1,x	; LSB 16-bit channel, update early here
			bcs cmd0b1adddone		; No overflow, done
			dec trackn_audf,x		; Decrement the MSB if the value went past #$00
cmd0b1subdone
			jmp pp9					; Done
		EIF

cmd0b2	; Sawtooth is so unlikely to even range the low #$FF frequencies that applying the vibrato fixes is pointless!
		IFT FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH&&FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
			cmp #$41				; 1.79mhz => Sawtooth?
			bne cmd0b3				; No Sawtooth for sure
			lda trackn_shiftfrq,x
			clc
			adc trackn_tablenote,x	; Here as a frequency
			clc
			adc (p_nr),y			; Note frequency table
			IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
				clc
				adc frqaddcmd2		; Possible shift by command 2
			EIF
			sta trackn_audf+2,x		; Since we're in channel 1 of either POKEY, offset +2 will always be the 3rd channel
			pla						; Get the second sawtooth pointer back from stack
			sta p_nr				; Update the tables pointer to the other sawtooth table
		EIF

cmd0b3
		lda trackn_shiftfrq,x		; Vibrato, and some other shifts use this value
		clc							; Clear carry
		adc trackn_tablenote,x		; freq table
		IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
			clc						; Clear carry
			adc frqaddcmd2			; If the CMD2 feature is also enabled, add that value as well
		EIF
		sta tmp						; Temporary, for faster operation below
cmd0b3a
		lda (p_nr),y				; This is the actual note base frequency, or AUDF
		clc							; Clear carry
		bpl cmd0b3c					; If the value is positive, branch and finish there
cmd0b3b
		adc tmp
		bvs cmd0c
		bmi cmd0c
		lda #$ff					; If overflow, force #$ff!
		bne cmd0c
cmd0b3c
		adc tmp
		bvs cmd0c
		bpl cmd0c
		lda #$00					; If overflow, force #$00!

	EIF								; FEAT_TABLETYPE

; CAUTION! Routine is not terminated, falls-through because the "jmp pp9" was removed.
cmd0c
	sta trackn_audf,x				; Store into audf

; End of instruments commands code.
; Falls trough to pp9

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of Portamento code... This is currently not properly compatible with 16-bit mode or Sawtooth, unfortunately.
; TODO: fix Portamento for things that use combined channels to run
; UPDATE: starting to understand a bit more how Portamento is working in the code...
; POTENTIAL IMPROVEMENT: process the command in a different order? Add CMD2 pitch, and Vibrato Fix?
; Maybe even set a flag to make sure the "reached" pitch clears the portamento mode?
; That way, it won't try to process it infinitely and possibly output incorrect pitch...

pp9
; Portamento effect processing
	IFT FEAT_PORTAMENTO
		lda trackn_portaspeeda,x	; Is the portamento effect curently active?
		beq pp10					; If $00, it is not active, so skip.
		dec trackn_portaspeeda,x	; Decrease the value by 1.
		bne pp10					; If not $00, it is still active, so skip.
		lda trackn_portaspeed,x		; Portamento speed in memory
		sta trackn_portaspeeda,x	; Overwrite the current portamento speed value to reset it
		lda trackn_portafrqa,x		; Current portamento frequency in memory
		cmp trackn_portafrqc,x		; Compare current portamento frequency to target frequency
		beq pp10					; If equal, portamento is done and can be skipped
		bcs pps1					; If the current portamento pitch is higher, branch to pps1

; Current portamento frequency < target frequency
		adc trackn_portadepth,x		; Add the portamento frequency offset to it.
		bcs pps8					; Overflow? Branch if the carry flag is set.
		cmp trackn_portafrqc,x		; Compare to the target portamento frequency.
		bcs pps8					; Equal or above means it was reached.
		jmp pps9					; Otherwise, it was not reached yet.

pps1
; Current portamento frequency > target frequency
		sbc trackn_portadepth,x		; Subtract the portamento frequency offset from it.
		bcc pps8					; Underflow? Branch if the carry flag is cleared.
		cmp trackn_portafrqc,x		; Compare to the target portamento frequency.
		bcs pps9					; Equal or above means it was not yet reached.

pps8								; After the subtraction it is already smaller
		lda trackn_portafrqc,x		; The target pitch was reached, load it in memory
pps9
		sta trackn_portafrqa,x		; Update the current portamento pitch with the new pitch
pp10
		lda reg2					; Get instrument command and distortion.
		and #$01					; Portamento is bit 0 in "0000 000s".
		beq pp11					; If $00, the flag is not set and portamento will be skipped

pp10a
;		lda trackn_portafrqa,x		; Load the current portamento frequency in memory
;		clc							; Clear the carry flag
;		adc trackn_shiftfrq,x		; add to it the shiftfrq/vibrato pitch

; TODO: add support for CMD2 offset, and fix vibrato when TableFreq is also involved, they have been ignored here!
; looks like the CMD0, and CMD1 were also ignored??? but why?
; seems like the Table of Freqs mode is broken? Adding Negative values

		lda trackn_shiftfrq,x		; Vibrato, and some other shifts use this value
		IFT FEAT_COMMAND2
			clc						; Clear carry
			adc frqaddcmd2			; If the CMD2 feature is also enabled, add that value as well
		EIF
		sta tmp						; Temporary, for faster operation below
		lda trackn_portafrqa,x		; Load the current portamento frequency in memory.
		clc							; Clear the carry flag.
		bpl pp10c 					; Positive value is outside of the dangerous range and can be processed
pp10b
		adc tmp
		bvs pp10d
		bmi pp10d
		lda #$ff					; If overflow, force #$ff!
		bne pp10d
pp10c
		adc tmp
		bvs pp10d
		bpl pp10d
		lda #0						; If overflow, force #$00!
pp10d

		sta trackn_audf,x			; Update the channel AUDF with the new value if portamento was processed.
pp11
	EIF

; End of Portamento code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Part of mainloop code.
; This is an extra step added for the purpose of clearning the memory from 16-bit or Sawtooth addresses when unused.

ppnext								; Jumped to when the instrument is not initialized
	dex								; OPTIMIZATION (x--)
	bmi rmt_p4						; OPTIMIZATION
	jmp pp1							; Loop

;---------------------------------------------------------------------


rmt_p4
	ldy #0							; Will be used to mute channels and reset the flags

; End of mainloop code... everything below will be conditionally assembled for easy optimization.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of 16-bit flag code... a much more stripped down version
; TODO: implement in a much more efficient way...
; BUG? LSB channels need to be reset to process certain commands properly? That doesn't sound right...

; UPDATE: this entire block may not even be necessary after all!
; It could be moved right in the channels index bit right where the initial flag check is done!
; UPDATE2: nevermind, this might fail on empty instrument channels, so better keep it here...

	IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16
bb1
		lda g_flag+1
		bpl bb2						; Not 16-bit flag, do nothing here
		lda trackn_bass16+0			; ch1
		sta trackn_audf+0
bb2
		lda g_flag+3
		bpl bb3						; Not 16-bit flag, do nothing here
		lda trackn_bass16+2			; ch3
		sta trackn_audf+2
bb3
		sty trackn_bass16+0
		sty trackn_bass16+2

		IFT STEREOMODE==1
bs1
			lda g_flag+1+4
			bpl bs2					; Not 16-bit flag, do nothing here
			lda trackn_bass16+0+4	; ch1
			sta trackn_audf+0+4
bs2
			lda g_flag+3+4
			bpl bs3					; Not 16-bit flag, do nothing here
			lda trackn_bass16+2+4	; ch3
			sta trackn_audf+2+4
bs3
			sty trackn_bass16+0+4
			sty trackn_bass16+2+4
		EIF
	EIF					; FEAT_FULL_16BIT||FEAT_BASS16

; End of 16-bit flag code...

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Additional operations for filters and 16-bit bass.
; A much more stripped down version.
; TODO: redesign the implementation to allow a much more precise manipulation to be achieved
; UPDATE: an attempt to mitigate overflows has been done here...

; Filters
	IFT FEAT_FILTER
		ldx v_audctl

		IFT FEAT_FILTERG0L			; Track 0/Channel 1 is filtered through channel 3
			lda trackn_command+0	; AUTOFILTER command bit 7 set for track 0?
			bpl qq2					; Bit 7 not set, no filtering.
			lda trackn_audc+0		; Get the current AUDC value from track 0.
			and #$0f				; Only keep the volume value from the byte
			beq qq2					; If the volume is 0, skip filtering,

									; With filtering
			lda trackn_audf+0		; Get the current AUDF value from track 0.
			clc						; Clear the carry flag.
			bpl qq1a				; It's alright! carry on if the value is in the positive range
			sta tmp					; Quick backup first
			adc trackn_filter+0		; Add the frequency shift offset for filtering.
			bmi qq1b				; All good, carry on!
			lda tmp					; Reload the backup value if it had overflown
			sec						; Set the carry flag first!
			sbc trackn_filter+0		; Subtract the frequency offset instead!
			bmi qq1b				; Finish like normal from here
qq1a
			adc trackn_filter+0		; Add the frequency offset for the AUTOFILTER modulation into the ch1 frequency
qq1b
			sta trackn_audf+2		; Set the new filter frequency.
			sty trackn_filter+0		; Reset that value until a new CMD6 overwrites it
qq1c
			txa						; Get the AUDCTL into the accumulator.
			ora #$04				; Set the AUDCTL High Pass Filter Ch1+3 bit 2.
			tax						; Transfer AUDCTL back into <X> to process the next channel the exact same way.
		EIF							; FEAT_FILTERG0L

qq2
		IFT FEAT_FILTERG1L
			lda trackn_command+1	; track1
			bpl qq3					; Top bit==0 => no filtering
			lda trackn_audc+1		; Take audc
			and #$0f				; Volume 0-15 only
			beq qq3					; Zero => no filtering

									; With filtering
			lda trackn_audf+1		; Frequency of g1
			clc
			bpl qq2a
			sta tmp
			adc trackn_filter+1		; Shift for filtering
			bmi qq2b
			lda tmp
			sec
			sbc trackn_filter+1
			bmi qq2b
qq2a
			adc trackn_filter+1
qq2b
			sta trackn_audf+3		; g1 is filtered through g3
			sty trackn_filter+1
qq2c
			txa						; Get the AUDCTL into the accumulator.
			ora #$02				; Set the AUDCTL High Pass Filter Ch2+4 bit 1.
			tax			 			; Transfer AUDCTL back into <X> to process the next channel the exact same way.

		EIF							; FEAT_FILTERG1L
qq3
		stx v_audctl
	EIF

	IFT FEAT_FILTER&&TRACKS>4
		ldx v_audctl2
qs1
		IFT FEAT_FILTERG0R
			lda trackn_command+0+4		; track0R
			bpl qs2						; Top bit==0 => no filtering
			lda trackn_audc+0+4			; Take audc
			and #$0f					; Volume 0-15 only
			beq qs2						; Zero => no filtering

										; With filtering
			lda trackn_audf+0+4			; Frequency of g0R
			clc
			bpl qs1a
			sta tmp
			adc trackn_filter+0+4		; Shift for filtering
			bmi qs1b
			lda tmp
			sec
			sbc trackn_filter+0+4
			bmi qs1b
qs1a
			adc trackn_filter+0+4
qs1b
			sta trackn_audf+2+4			; g0R is filtered through g2R
			sty trackn_filter+0+4
qs1c
			txa
			ora #4						; bit2 audctl (filter g0-g2)
			tax
		EIF	; FEAT_FILTERG0R
qs2
		IFT FEAT_FILTERG1R
			lda trackn_command+1+4		; track1R
			bpl qs3						; Top bit==0 => no filtering
			lda trackn_audc+1+4			; Take audc
			and #$0f					; Volume 0-15 only
			beq qs3						; Zero => no filtering

										; With filtering
			lda trackn_audf+1+4			; Frequency of g1R
			clc
			bpl qs2a
			sta tmp
			adc trackn_filter+1+4		; Shift for filtering
			bmi qs2b
			lda tmp
			sec
			sbc trackn_filter+1+4
			bmi qs2b
qs2a
			adc trackn_filter+1+4
qs2b
			sta trackn_audf+3+4			; g1R is filtered through g3R
			sty trackn_filter+1+4
qs2c
			txa
			ora #$02					; bit1 audctl (filter g1-g3)
			tax
		EIF	; FEAT_FILTERG1R
qs3
		stx v_audctl2
	EIF

; End of Autofilter code...

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; End of mainloop code, hit that RTS and that's it!

rmt_p5
	rts

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of the sawtooth code. There is room for improvements.

	IFT FEAT_FULL_SAWTOOTH&&FEAT_AUDCTLMANUALSET
do_sawtooth
		IFT FEAT_FILTER
			eor #$80				; Inverts the AUTOFILTER bit, so it does not overwrite things later
			sta trackn_command,x	; Overwrite the command byte before the AUTOFILTER code since things where done early
		EIF
		lda #$64					; High pass filter, CH1+3 + 1.79mhz CH1+3
		IFT TRACKS>4				; Stereo mode
			cpx #4					; Are we in the right POKEY channels?
			bcc do_sawtooth_a 		; If x is lower than 4, we are not
			ora v_audctl2			; Combine the existing AUDCTL value to it
			sta v_audctl2			; Store the new AUDCTL value, right POKEY
			bne do_sawtooth_b 		; Unconditional
		EIF
do_sawtooth_a
		ora v_audctl				; Combine the existing AUDCTL value to it
		sta v_audctl				; Store the new AUDCTL value, left POKEY
do_sawtooth_b

		IFT FEAT_COMMAND6			; Sawtooth CMD6 hack... could be optimized much better, or maybe moved into the commands?
			lda reg2				; Command and Distortion
			and #$70				; Keep the Command bits only
			cmp #$60				; CMD6?
			bne do_sawtooth_c 		; Skip if not equal
			lda reg3				; $XY parameter
			beq do_sawtooth_c 		; Skip if the value is 0, nothing will be changed
			bmi sawtooth_reverse	; Negative values (#$80 to #$FF) will reverse the pointers, positive values (#$01 to #$7F) will set the pointers back to normal
sawtooth_normal
			lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch1
			sta saw_ch1
			lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch3
			sta saw_ch3
			bpl do_sawtooth_c
sawtooth_reverse
			lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch3
			sta saw_ch1
			lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch1
			sta saw_ch3
		EIF

do_sawtooth_c
		lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch1
saw_ch1	equ *-1
		pha							; Very TEMPORARILY keep the other pointer in the stack
		lda #<frqtabsawtooth_ch3
saw_ch3	equ *-1
		sta p_nr
		inc reg1					; #$40 => #$41, will be necessary later to help differentiate the other flags!
do_sawtooth_d
		lda #>PAGE_EXTRA_0			; Tables MSB pointer, it's the same one regardless of the table used
		jmp store_tables_lsb_a		; Finish in the middle of the 64khz/1.79mhz branch

	EIF								; FEAT_FILTER

; End of the sawtooth code.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Start of 16-bit bass (BASS16) code.

	IFT FEAT_BASS16
do_bass16
		IFT TRACKS>4				; Stereo mode
			cpx #4					; Are we in the right POKEY channels?
			bcc do_bass16_a 		; If x is lower than 4, we are not
			ora v_audctl2			; Merge the values with the AUDCTL in memory
			sta v_audctl2			; Overwrite the AUDCTL, to force 16-bit mode through Distortion 6
			bne do_bass16_b			; Unconditional
		EIF
do_bass16_a
		ora v_audctl				; Merge the values with the AUDCTL in memory
		sta v_audctl				; Overwrite the AUDCTL, to force 16-bit mode through Distortion 6
do_bass16_b
		lda #$80 					; 16-bit pointer
		sta g_flag,x				; Flag set in the MSB channel --actually necessary since the flag is retrieved later!
		sta reg1					; Since it is not permanent, it is good for immediate use!
		eor #$FF 					; Invert, #$80 becomes #$7F
		sta g_flag-1,x				; Flag set for the next channel, which will be skipped due to being in 16-bit mode now!
do_bass16_c
		IFT FEAT_COMMAND6&&FEAT_FULL_16BIT
			lda reg2				; Distortion and Commands
			and #$70				; Leave only the Commands bits
			cmp #$60				; CMD6?
			bne do_bass16_d			; Skip if not CMD6
			lda reg3				; XY parameter
			and #$0E				; Mask with "%000ddd0", strip away all unwanted bits so the left nibble will not affect anything
			sta bass16_pointer		; PERMANENTLY change the value until a new CMD6 value is read
		EIF
		IFT FEAT_FULL_16BIT
do_bass16_d
			ldy #$0A				; Distortion A
bass16_pointer equ *-1
			lda reg1				; The flag has been set, and also became the tables pointer!
			jmp store_tables_lsb	; Continue like normal from there

		ELS			; FIXMEEEE... later
			lda #<frqtabpure_hi
			sta p_nr
			lda #<frqtabpure_lo
			sta trackn_bass16
			lda #0
			sta trackn_audc-1,x		; Update the next channel's AUDC early, it will always be volume 0, and Distortion won't matter
			lda #>PAGE_DISTORTION_A
			sta trackn_bass16+1		; This value can also be used to identify if 16-bit mode is active or not, since it will never be 0
			sta p_nr+1
			lda tmp
			ora #$A0
			jmp store_tables_lsb_c
		EIF

	EIF

; End of the 16-bit bass (BASS16) code.


;	END
;==========================================================================================

; Start of the rmt_set_pokey routine to update the POKEY hardware registers.
rmt_set_pokey

	ldy #$00
v_audctl equ *-1				; Left POKEY AUDCTL is loaded as the very first thing, for all STEREOMODE variations

	IFT STEREOMODE==1			; L1 L2 L3 L4 R1 R2 R3 R4
								; Write to the two POKEYs, stereo (always the right register first, then immediately the left)

		lda trackn_audf+0+4		; AUDF0
		ldx trackn_audf+0
		sta pokey_right+$0
		stx pokey_left+$0
		lda trackn_audc+0+4		; AUDC0
		ldx trackn_audc+0
		sta pokey_right+$1
		stx pokey_left+$1

		lda trackn_audf+1+4		; AUDF1
		ldx trackn_audf+1
		sta pokey_right+$2
		stx pokey_left+$2

		lda trackn_audc+1+4		; AUDC1
		ldx trackn_audc+1
		sta pokey_right+$3
		stx pokey_left+$3

		lda trackn_audf+2+4		; AUDF2
		ldx trackn_audf+2
		sta pokey_right+$4
		stx pokey_left+$4

		lda trackn_audc+2+4		; AUDC2
		ldx trackn_audc+2
		sta pokey_right+$5
		stx pokey_left+$5

		lda trackn_audf+3+4		; AUDF3
		ldx trackn_audf+3
		sta pokey_right+$6
		stx pokey_left+$6

		lda trackn_audc+3+4		; AUDC3
		ldx trackn_audc+3
		sta pokey_right+$7
		stx pokey_left+$7

		lda #$00				; AUDCTL
v_audctl2 equ *-1
		sta pokey_right+$8
		sty pokey_left+$8		; <Y> was set above.

		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
			lda #$03
v_skctl equ *-1
			ldy #$03
v_skctl2 equ *-1
			sty pokey_right+$f
			sta pokey_left+$f
		EIF
	ELI STEREOMODE==0			; L1 L2 L3 L4
		lda trackn_audf+0
		ldx trackn_audc+0
		sta pokey_left+$0
		stx pokey_left+$1

		lda trackn_audf+1
		ldx trackn_audc+1
		sta pokey_left+$0+2
		stx pokey_left+$1+2

		lda trackn_audf+2
		ldx trackn_audc+2
		sta pokey_left+$0+4
		stx pokey_left+$1+4

		lda trackn_audf+3
		ldx trackn_audc+3
		sta pokey_left+$0+6
		stx pokey_left+$1+6

		sty pokey_left+$8

		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
			lda #$03
v_skctl equ *-1
			sta pokey_left+$f
		EIF
	ELI STEREOMODE==2			; L1 R2 R3 L4
		lda trackn_audf+0
		ldx trackn_audc+0
		sta pokey_left+$0
		stx pokey_left+$1
		sta pokey_right+$0		; The frequency into the right one too (in case R2 plays 16-bit bass 2+1)

		lda trackn_audf+1
		ldx trackn_audc+1
		sta pokey_right+$0+2
		stx pokey_right+$1+2

		lda trackn_audf+2
		ldx trackn_audc+2
		sta pokey_right+$0+4
		stx pokey_right+$1+4
		sta pokey_left+$0+4		; The frequency into the left one too (in case L1 plays filter 1+3 or L4 plays 16-bit bass 4+3)

		lda trackn_audf+3
		ldx trackn_audc+3
		sta pokey_left+$0+6
		stx pokey_left+$1+6
		sta pokey_right+$0+6	; The frequency into the right one too (in case R2 plays filter 2+4)

		sty pokey_right+$8
		sty pokey_left+$8

		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
			lda #$03
v_skctl equ *-1
			sta pokey_left+$f
			sta pokey_right+$f
		EIF
	ELI STEREOMODE==3			; L1 L2 R3 R4
		lda trackn_audf+0
		ldx trackn_audc+0
		sta pokey_left+$0
		stx pokey_left+$1

		lda trackn_audf+1
		ldx trackn_audc+1
		sta pokey_left+$0+2
		stx pokey_left+$1+2

		lda trackn_audf+2
		ldx trackn_audc+2
		sta pokey_right+$0+4
		stx pokey_right+$1+4
		sta pokey_left+$0+4		; The frequency into the left one too (in case L1 plays filter 1+3)

		lda trackn_audf+3
		ldx trackn_audc+3
		sta pokey_right+$0+6
		stx pokey_right+$1+6
		sta pokey_left+$0+6		; The frequency into the left one too (in case L2 plays filter 2+4)

		sty pokey_right+$8
		sty pokey_left+$8

		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
			lda #$03
v_skctl equ *-1
			sta pokey_left+$f
			sta pokey_right+$f
		EIF

	ELI STEREOMODE==4			; LR1 LR2 LR3 LR4
		lda trackn_audf+0
		ldx trackn_audc+0
		sta pokey_left+$0
		stx pokey_left+$1
		sta pokey_right+$0
		stx pokey_right+$1
		lda trackn_audf+1
		ldx trackn_audc+1
		sta pokey_left+$0+2
		stx pokey_left+$1+2
		sta pokey_right+$0+2
		stx pokey_right+$1+2
		lda trackn_audf+2
		ldx trackn_audc+2
		sta pokey_left+$0+4
		stx pokey_left+$1+4
		sta pokey_right+$0+4
		stx pokey_right+$1+4
		lda trackn_audf+3
		ldx trackn_audc+3
		sta pokey_left+$0+6
		stx pokey_left+$1+6
		sta pokey_right+$0+6
		stx pokey_right+$1+6

		sty pokey_left+$8
		sty pokey_right+$8

		IFT FEAT_TWO_TONE
			lda #$03
v_skctl equ *-1
			sta pokey_left+$f
			sta pokey_right+$f
		EIF
	EIF

	rts

; End of the rmt_set_pokey routine.

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

RMTPLAYEREND

; Player ends here, what lies after is anything you want, and the extra workaround code if assembled as a 'tracker.obx' binary

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; Let's not forget the tables and other RMT data!
	icl "rmtdata.a65"

;---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------;

; The workaround code is mandatory in order to avoid many things breaking in RMT!
	IFT FEAT_IS_TRACKER
		icl "rmtextra.a65"
	EIF
